ly in the replacement namespace and no receipt exists under the original held directory. Check verifies the original handle IDs against themselves, not the current selected pathname. Metadata-only directory handles therefore do not provide the promised final-directory rename exclusion on this Windows environment.", "fix": "Keep selected namespace and actual child opens bound to the same native directory identity throughout the operation. Use a native handle/access/open strategy that demonstrably excludes rename/replacement, or open children relative to a validated retained directory handle with an equivalent namespace guarantee. Fail closed on drift; a saved handle ID or a pathname check without continuous binding is insufficient. Add the deterministic final-directory replacement regression and retain separate source-file write/flush/read continuity checks.", "minimal_fix_paths": ["adapters/runtime/qualification_failure_proof_windows.go", "adapters/runtime/qualification_failure_proof_windows_test.go"], "limits": "Owned fresh fixture and unexported production helpers through Go overlay; no actual cross-user attacker or original/production path was exercised. Ancestor root rename was denied in initial cut; selected final directory replacement succeeded. Separate native file handles correctly refused competing writes/deletes/renames."}, {"id": "B-r2-F02", "priority": "P1", "prior_finding": "B-F03 raw/native consumer evidence requirement remains incomplete", "title": "Private consumer accepts changed original native files after closure", "path": "internal/domain/runtime_qualification_failure_windows.go", "lines": [857, 884], "evidence": ["B-r2-review-014.stdout.txt", "independent_b2_domain_windows_test.go"], "detail": "A real controlled-loopback native qualification first-gate denial completed and validatedQualificationFailureTx passed. Each of stdout.raw, stderr.raw, bridge.json and the original qualification-rejection JSON was then independently changed on disk, with sealed marker, proof and all database rows unchanged. The actual private consumer still returned a closure for all four cuts. The native source reader independently rejected the first three damaged files. MODEL Host fact is reopened, but consumer lines 857-860 only cross-check native hashes already stored inside proof/observation; the native terminal files and original rejection are not reloaded and bound to those seals.", "fix": "At actual private transaction consumption, freshly read protected original native files through the corrected namespace/identity guard; compare journal/stdout/stderr/raw rejection and exact frame/payload/ACK/subject facts against the sealed proof, marker and current dispatch. Recompute raw digests and canonical object hashes at their proper boundaries and refuse absence/drift. The completed-marker path should consume this same full validation. Add post-closure individual native-file/refusal tamper tests retaining unchanged DB/proof/marker positive controls.", "minimal_fix_paths": ["internal/domain/runtime_qualification_failure_windows.go", "internal/domain/runtime_qualification_failure_windows_test.go"], "limits": "This reproduces direct private-consumer acceptance, not an arbitrary production SQL capability. Existing closeOnlineQualificationFailure re-reads native files before the completed-marker branch and refuses malformed inputs there; post-tamper successful replay is not claimed. Correct-baseline actual closure replay was exercised and had zero logical delta."}], "prior_finding_disposition": {"B-F01": "PARTIAL: native ACL/owner/file checks improve privacy and reject Everyone; final-directory namespace binding still fails B-r2-F01.", "B-F02": "REPAIR_SUPPORTED: original base-f48 ordinary test body and helper fully restored; diff only appends registry tests; fresh original three groups and two claim-order subtests pass with zero SKIP.", "B-F03": "PARTIAL: exact MODEL history/Host fact and independently mutated receipt/request/hash/route/credential/key/history controls now reject; full native seal revalidation remains B-r2-F02."}, "coverage": {"full_nine": "Frozen manifest nine SHA256 values verified in command018; worktree clean, source_final_verification.json; four integration deltas reviewed with caller neighborhoods.", "five_delta": "Exact five source/test paths from 75e5257c verified in command018; no source changes made.", "first_gate": "Command008 fresh valid synthetic gate seed plus 24 isolated mutation cases; controlled native LIVE-mode fixture reaches broker before prepareEffectTx; one loopback MODEL, raw3 ACK2 rejected1, no TOOL effect; original raw queue_empty semantics preserved while Host derivation closes FAILED.", "ordinary_mu": "Command009 three original groups, two claim subtests, zero skip; actual existing local pinned Mu SDK bundle; same process/cancellation/recovery/claim assertions preserved.", "native_acl": "Commands006/014: current owner safe full access and generic all accepted; Everyone direct/inherited/source file, WRITE_DAC/generic rights, INHERIT_ONLY owner and unsupported deny/System ACE rejected conservatively. Source-file competing write/delete/rename blocked and write+flush+read bytes preserved in command016. Namespace failure separate.", "model_binding": "Command008 author suite freshly rerun, plus seven independent command014 DB cuts with a baseline private consumer and rollback checks. Host model raw response digest and receipt id tied to SSE; domain Hash operates on canonical object serialization while Digest hashes original bytes. Receipt/request proof must still include full native revalidation.", "transaction_and_replay": "Independent command014 captures 87 non-sqlite application tables before/after actual closure; only nine expected tables change, exactly five added domain_versions kinds (Artifact, ImpactLink, Run, ProjectState, EventEnvelope) and one uploaded_content row. Actual closeOnlineQualificationFailure completed-marker branch replay returns zero lo